Checker v2 refuses five writes that v1 accepts (ownership-v2.md §2.11.5, the record pass; #2480). `inline`: the schema value is an earlier operand of the call that takes the updated copy, and v2 takes it to hold the copy (`held-operand`). `after`, `listAfter` and `pushed`: `Schema.decode` or `Schema.read` took a schema value before, and v2 refuses each later write of the declaration (`escaped`): of a copy and of a list that are made after that call, and of a parameter that the call did not take. `parsed`: the record is a parse's answer, and v2 refuses the callee's write of it (`unknown`, approximate). Each is an over-refusal of v2. v2 cannot identify a schema member until S7 builds schemas (#1020), and it reads `Schema.decode` as pessimistic until S6 reads core's contracts (#1704). `alone` has no schema member, and both checkers accept it.
